     "stop_timestamp": "2025-10-24T02:05:14.897000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Before writing it, check one thing: the posted hours on the Perry Street lot sign. If it says enforcement ends at 7:00 pm, that's your strongest argument by far, stronger than the permit visibility point.\n\nDraft (assuming enforcement ends at 7 pm):\n\n> I am appealing citation #[number], issued on October 21, 2025 at 7:52 pm in the Perry Street lot.\n>\n> The posted signage for this lot states that permits are required until 7:00 pm. The citation was issued after enforcement hours, so no permit was required at that time.\n>\n> In addition, I hold a valid graduate parking permit (#[number]), which was displayed on the dashboard at the time. I have attached a photo of the permit and the lot signage.\n>\n> I respectfully request that the citation be dismissed.\n\nAttach: a photo of the sign with the hours, a photo of your permit, and your permit number.",
     "citations": []
    }
